enied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md:occ-c95136f3aa5b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":135},"excerpt":"…in BCO 24-1 a. thru e., and the characteristics of a Deacon described in BCO 9-3. In the reasoning and opinion of the SJC, there is no mention that any member of the Midway Session judged Mr. Crouse to be deficient in any of the Biblical or…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["deacon re-election","eligibility for office","session discretion","de facto deposition","retaliation for complaint","standard of review","BCO 39-3 deference","right to file complaint","officer nomination","candidate eligibility"],"standard_of_review":"discretion_and_judgment","review_standards":["discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2019-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A complaint challenging a session's refusal to advance an ordained deacon's nomination for re-election to the diaconate was denied by the SJC. Northwest Georgia Presbytery had adopted its judicial commission's judgment that the session did not err; applying BCO 39-3(3)'s deference to discretionary judgments, the SJC found no clear error, held formal charges were unnecessary and re-election was not guaranteed, and refused to attribute one elder's questionable retaliation rationale to the session. The majority encouraged prompt communication of reasons. A dissent would apply BCO 39-3.4 and sustain."}},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Brown v. Northern California Presbytery","year":2011,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-420bcfa8c218","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":380},"excerpt":"…Diaconate of a new Church includes two Deaconesses commissioned contrary to BCO 9-3.\" The following year, the 36th GA found their response unsatisfactory, expanding on the reasoning from the 35th GA as follows:","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-8b4c6365b9a1","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":382},"excerpt":"…the Session, not Members of a Diaconate (Board of Deacons, 9-4). According to BCO 9-3 and 9-4, a Diaconate may only include men who are elected, ordained and installed. Therefore, the body referenced in the exception must not be called a Diaconate. In…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["diaconate","deaconess","women in church office","in thesi statement","abstract decree","presbyterial jurisdiction","BCO 9-7","appointed deaconess","elected deaconess","equal partners","nobody ordained","GUMP standard","Kniseley standard"],"case_numbers":["2009-26"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Joined with Case 2009-25; the Session of Grace Presbyterian Church complained that views 3, 4, 5, and 6 in Northern California Presbytery's resolution on diaconal practice violated the BCO. The SJC sustained the complaint on the same grounds as 2009-25, annulling the abstract resolution while declining to rule on the constitutional merits of any specific diaconal view."}},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"David Kniseley et al. v. Rocky Mountain Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-4de1dab42e51","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["minister title","non-ordained staff","women","constitutional interpretation","presbytery judgment"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-13"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"On complaint from TE David Kniseley and others, the SJC reviewed Rocky Mountain Presbytery's refusal to forbid a mission church from giving an unordained female staff member the title 'Minister of Church Life.' The SJC denied the complaint. It held the BCO uses 'minister' synonymously with pastor and teaching elder, but is silent on general use for non-ordained staff; a lower court may exercise discretion subject to BCO 40-2(3)'s WESP review. The decision addressed only the constitutional issue, not the title's wisdom or propriety; four commissioners dissented."}},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Mark Grasso et al. v. Philadelphia Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-e6b4608fbd42","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["ordination","licensure","women deacons","stated difference","confessional subscription"],"case_numbers":["2008-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The Session of Crossroads Community Church challenged Philadelphia Presbytery's licensing and ordination of a candidate who stated a difference concerning women and the office of deacon but agreed to follow the BCO. The SJC denied the complaint and affirmed Presbytery's judgment; a dissent argued it should have been sustained."}},{"id":"bco:9-3--overture:ga20_1992:33","record_id":"overture:ga20_1992:33","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 24-5 to Permit Session to Ordain Elders & Deacons","year":1992,"disposition":"Approved & ratified (1993)","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga20_1992.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga20_1992.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--overture:ga20_1992:33:occ-25fb0e1af3c0","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga20_1992.html#ga20-p118","repository_path":"markdown/ga20_1992.md#ga20-p118","locator":{"fragment":"ga20-p118","page":118},"excerpt":"…exemplary lives, brotherly spirit, warm sympathies, and sound judgment.\" BCO 9-3; and Whereas, it may be desirable in some instances to have greater participation of ruling elders in the ordination and installation of ruling elders and deacons; and…","sources":["overture_body_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga20_1992.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"source":"OVERTURE 33 from New River Presbytery (to CCB & B&O)"}},{"id":"bco:9-3--overture:ga19_1991:22","record_id":"overture:ga19_1991:22","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 24-5 to Permit Session to Ordain Elders & Deacons","year":1991,"disposition":"Carried over","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga19_1991.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga19_1991.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--overture:ga19_1991:22:occ-b8ffe620dca1","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/